# Fetched at build time by scripts/fetch-ollama-runtime.mjs — never commit
# vendored runtime binaries (see docs/DEPENDENCY_BUNDLING_PLAN.md). The
# directory itself must stay tracked (src-tauri/vendor/ollama/.gitkeep) —
# tauri-build validates bundle.resources paths exist on EVERY cargo
# invocation (check/test/clippy/build), not only `tauri build`'s actual
# bundling step, so a fully-gitignored directory breaks plain `cargo check`
# for every contributor who hasn't run the fetch script. Learned this the
# hard way via a real CI failure (see docs/DEPENDENCY_BUNDLING_PLAN.md's
# Implementation log) — do not re-ignore the directory itself again.
src-tauri/vendor/ollama/*
!src-tauri/vendor/ollama/.gitkeep
